    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. when you mention \"community cohesion\" being tied to things like local business density or property trends... how would you actually implement that in the model? like, if we see a neighborhood with a lot of transient populations or a high turnover of small businesses, would that be a signal for higher risk? i'm trying to understand if certain demographic mixes or types of local commerce serve as effective indicators for predicting default rates.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
