      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. so if we're using zip codes or business turnover as proxies for this \"fragility,\" aren't we basically just flagging certain types of neighborhoods? specifically, in many urban areas, those patterns of high turnover and transient populations also correlate heavily with specific ethnic or minority demographics. how do we balance the need for \"predictive accuracy\" with the risk that these neighborhood metrics act as a backdoor for racial profiling in the scoring? do you think the model will end up just penalizing certain communities for their socioeconomic landscape?",
